Japanese pronunciation-neighbor ordering and the offline comparison in
artifacts/pronunciation-neighbors-212/ use acoustic-distance CSV tables from
Jiro Shimaya's kanasim,
revision f067a4e8be10d818b37b8b9f08de933dae01524b, under Apache-2.0.
Source: https://github.com/jiroshimaya/kanasim
The unchanged production source tables and full upstream license are preserved
in content/pronunciation-neighbors/kanasim/. The derived weighting recipe and
provenance are documented in content/pronunciation-neighbors/README.md; historical
experiment inputs retain their separate copy and provenance in the artifact's
vendor/ directory. Source tables are used only during offline preparation; the
browser receives compact neighbor indices rather than acoustic tables or model
weights.
